    "guidance": "Lower-priority specialist, not a default: it passed the final skill exit in 5/12 in-distribution runs. Its object-frame target prior is intended for reliable block-position displacement, but that benefit has no out-of-distribution validation. Use only with drawer open/stable, a reliable low block pose, and an open gripper free of the handle; prefer h02 for a near-nominal block with unusual TCP/configuration and h03 when low-clearance ordering is the concern. Avoid with noisy/dropped object pose, displaced tunnel/drawer, or questionable reachability/collision clearance. Monitor for fingers closing without persistent object/TCP coupling, an open gripper, a low/stationary block, premature low transfer, drawer falling to <=0.26, or repeated IK nonconvergence/limit contacts. Validation showed nonzero IK-unconverged steps in 10/12 runs, and all seven final failures had an earlier first-pass step, so do not treat a transient exit observation as maintained success. Hand off in the supervised 680:840 overlap only after the block is outside the tunnel with its bottom above the 0.16 m roof (or already in the drawer), drawer_position remains >0.26, closed-finger object/TCP coupling persists, and motion has turned toward target_pose."
